N2  - Introduction: Tumor-associated tertiary lymphoid structures (TLS) have been reported to associate with favorable prognosis in most solid tumors including non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). However, the prognostic value of TLSs in resected NSCLC receiving preoperative neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy remain further investigation. Methods: We retrospectively included 98 patients with resected NSCLC from two cohorts based on neoadjuvant treatment: neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy(N=57), and neoadjuvant chemotherapy (N=41). TLSs were identified and quantified by H&amp;E staining of serial paraffin sections with a thickness of 3-5μm. Then TLS scoring system were established for inside tumor bed region (IT score) and outside tumor bed region (OT score). Multiplex immunohistochemistry (mIHC) was applied to characterize TLS maturation. Correlation between TLS and clinical outcomes including recurrence-free survival (RFS) and overall survival (OS) were analyzed by Kaplan-Meier estimator and Cox proportional hazards regression model. Results: Generally, the TLS density is higher in neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy cohort than that of neoadjuvant chemotherapy cohort (p<0.05). Patients with higher TLS density inside tumor bed region showed more favorable prognosis in both neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy cohort and neoadjuvant chemotherapy cohort, while TLS density outside tumor bed showed no significant correlation with clinical outcomes in either cohort. Furthermore, the multiplex immunohistochemistry analysis demonstrated both primary (CD21+CD23-) TLS and mature (CD21+CD23+) TLS were higher in neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy cohort than that of neoadjuvant chemotherapy cohort (p<0.05). TLS maturation was proved to be an independent predictor for RFS in the neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy cohort rather than neoadjuvant chemotherapy cohort. Conclusions: The density, spatial distribution and maturation of tertiary lymphoid structures are significantly associated with clinical outcomes and potentially provide valuable predicting factor for RFS in resectable NSCLC with neoadjuvant chemoimmunotherapy. [Formula presented] [Formula presented] Keywords: Tertiary lymphoid structures, Non-small cell lung cancer, Neoadjuvant
