N2  - Introduction: Recent studies have shown the association between gut microbiota and the pathogenesis of NSCLC. We aimed to assess the potential effects of combining neoadjuvant immunochemotherapy and probiotic supplements as a therapeutic strategy in NSCLC. Methods: In this real-world single-center prospective study, eligible patients with stage IIB to IIIB NSCLC received 3 cycles of nivolumab plus platinum-based chemotherapy and daily oral administration of probiotic supplements containing Bifidobacterium, Lactobacillus acidophilus, and Enterococcus faecalis, followed by resection. The primary endpoint was pathological complete response (pCR), and the second endpoint was progression-free survival (PFS). Gut microbiota of propensity-score-matched patients from pCR and non-pCR groups was analyzed using metagenomics sequencing. Results: Between August 2020 and June 2022, 43 patients were enrolled and received neoadjuvant treatment. At the time of data cutoff, the median duration of follow-up was 19.0 months. All 43 patients had tumour resection, 23 of whom (53.5%) achieved pCR. At 19 months, PFS was 93.0% (95% CI 81.4-97.6). While 42 (97.7%) of 43 patients had treatment-related adverse events (trAE) during neoadjuvant treatment, only 6 (14.0%) had trAE of grade 3, and none of the adverse events were associated with surgery delays or deaths. The beta diversity index of gut microbiota was elevated after receiving neoadjuvant immunochemotherapy plus probiotic supplements, but the chao1 index remained similar. The microbiome structures at species level significantly varied from pCR group to non-pCR group. There were 81 differentially-abundant microbial species before neoadjuvant treatment and 83 after neoadjuvant treatment between two groups, with 3 overlapping species including Legionella jordanis, Thiomonas intermedia, and Xanthomonas vasicola. Conclusions: Patients with stage IIB-IIIB NSCLC who received neoadjuvant immunochemotherapy plus probiotic supplements had a high pCR rate, a long PFS, and a low incidence of severe trAE. Gut microbiota may be involved in response to neoadjuvant immunochemotherapy in NSCLC, which requires further investigation. [Formula presented] [Formula presented] Keywords: non-small cell lung cancer, neoadjuvant immunochemotherapy, probiotic supplements
